{
  "rationale": "The plant automata G1 models the robot's perception (obstacle and marker sensing) and motion actuation. The specification automata E1 binds sensor outcomes to safe and goal-directed actions, enforcing safety (obstacle avoidance), marker search/tracking, and terminal stop on goal. E2 enforces that after obstacle recovery, a scan/search is performed before resuming forward or marker approach, preventing unsafe immediate forward motion. E3 ensures that only one controllable action is enabled per state, preventing oscillation and non-determinism.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automaton for perception and actuation, with all uncontrollable and controllable events.",
    "Specification automata encode safe action bindings, marker tracking/search, and recovery/scan policies."
  ],
